[Event "Modern Benoni"]

{The Benoni gives up central space for a queenside majority and an active g7-bishop.}
1. d4 {Claims the centre: the pawn on d4 controls c5 and e5. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1 and the queen on d1.}
1... Nf6 {Develops the knight to f6, where it controls e4 and d5.}
2. c4 {Space. Supports the centre: the pawn on c4 controls b5 and d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1.}
2... c5 {[%cal Gc5d4] The Benoni. Supports the centre: the pawn on c5 controls b4 and eyes the pawn on d4. It also opens a line for the queen on d8.}
3. d5 {Gains space. Claims the centre: the pawn on d5 controls c6 and e6.}
3... e6 {Opens lines. Supports the centre: the pawn on e6 controls f5 and eyes the pawn on d5. It also opens a line for the bishop on f8.}
4. Nc3 {Develops the knight to c3, where it controls e4 and supports the pawn on d5.}
4... exd5 {Takes the pawn on d5; White will want to recapture.}
5. cxd5 {Recaptures on d5, restoring the material balance.}
5... d6 {Supports the centre: the pawn on d6 controls e5 and supports the pawn on c5. It also opens a line for the bishop on c8.}
6. e4 {Claims the centre: the pawn on e4 controls f5 and supports the pawn on d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1 and the bishop on f1.}
 (6. Nf3 {Develops the knight to f3, where it controls e5 and d4.}
6... g6 {Fianchetto. The pawn on g6 controls f5 and h5.}
7. g3 {Fianchetto. The pawn on g3 controls f4 and h4.}
7... Bg7 {Fianchettoes the bishop on g7, where it rakes the long diagonal through f6. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
8. Bg2 {Long diagonal. Fianchettoes the bishop on g2, where it rakes the long diagonal through f3. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
8... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
9. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
9... Na6 {Heads for c7. Develops the knight to a6, where it supports the pawn on c5.}
)
6... g6 {Fianchetto. The pawn on g6 controls f5 and h5.}
7. Nf3 {Develops the knight to f3, where it controls e5 and d4.}
 (7. f4 {The Taimanov. Supports the centre: the pawn on f4 controls e5 and g5.}
7... Bg7 {Fianchettoes the bishop on g7, where it rakes the long diagonal through f6. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
8. Bb5+ {Checks. It is check, so the reply is forced. Develops the bishop to b5, where it controls c6 and c4. It gives check.}
8... Nfd7 {Blocks. Regroups the knight to d7 and controls e5.}
9. a4 {Stops ...a6 and ...b5. Gains space on the queenside; the pawn on a4 takes b5 away from the opponent.}
)
7... Bg7 {Fianchettoes the bishop on g7, where it rakes the long diagonal through f6. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
8. Be2 {Develops the bishop to e2, where it controls d3 and supports the knight on f3. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
8... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
9. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
9... Re8 {Hits e4. The rook goes to e8 and controls e5 and eyes the pawn on e4.}
 (9... a6 {Prepares ...b5. The pawn on a6 controls b5.}
10. a4 {Stops ...b5. Gains space on the queenside; the pawn on a4 takes b5 away from the opponent.}
)
10. Nd2 {Supports e4. Regroups the knight to d2 and supports the pawn on e4.}
10... Na6 {Heads for c7. Develops the knight to a6, where it supports the pawn on c5.}
 (10... Nbd7 {Heads for e5. Develops the knight to d7, where it controls e5.}
11. a4 {Stops ...b5. Gains space on the queenside; the pawn on a4 takes b5 away from the opponent.}
) *
